.TH TERRY-DICE 1 "October 2026" "ALI Linux 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
terry-dice \- the ALI security base: real random rolls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B terry-dice hex
.RI [ bytes ]
.br
.B terry-dice id
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each roll hashes machine stats (RAM x disk + RAM, uptime, boot
id, load) with 32 fresh kernel-CSPRNG bytes. Stats make it yours,
the kernel makes it unguessable. Refuses to roll without kernel
entropy.
.B id
prints the stable machine ID (first roll kept).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ali-passgen (1),
.BR ali-vault (1)
